# Cloudflare Pages headers config: https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/
#
# ── Security headers (all pages) ──────────────────────────────────
# Content-Security-Policy is NOT set here any more (security assessment
# 2026-09, R4): it is per-page — each page's inline <script> blocks are
# hashed at build time (scripts/gen-csp.js → src/csp-hashes.json) and the
# Worker attaches the matching policy to every HTML response (src/lib/csp.js,
# applied in src/index.js's catch-all). That policy has no 'unsafe-inline'
# for scripts; inline on*="…" handlers were replaced by the data-action
# delegation in public/theme.js and the Tailwind Play CDN by a static build.
# A value that differs per page can't be expressed in this file.
#
# NOTE: Cache-Control is deliberately NOT set here. Two things were tried and
# both failed to actually take effect, verified against live response
# headers each time:
#   1. Separate `/*.js` / `/*.css` blocks — Cloudflare Pages' _headers path
#      matching doesn't support extension globs like that; it doesn't error,
#      it just silently never matches anything.
#   2. Cache-Control inside this same `/*` block — this pattern IS confirmed
#      to work (every other header here does reach .js/.css requests), but
#      Cloudflare Pages overrides Cache-Control specifically with its own
#      default asset policy (`max-age=14400`, ~4h) regardless.
# The actual fix lives in src/index.js's final catch-all: the Worker rewrites
# Cache-Control on the response itself after env.ASSETS.fetch() returns,
# which isn't subject to whatever Pages does internally with this file. See
# the comment there for why this matters (issue #33 — entotools.com and
# entotools.org, as separate custom domains on the same deployment, cache
# independently, so a stale edge cache on one could keep serving an old
# APP_VERSION for hours after a deploy).
/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=(), interest-cohort=()
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
